KAYTX AI WORKFORCE - COMPLETE DATABASE WITH SUB-AGENTS (900+ Agents)
================================================================================
Each Main Agent now has 2-4 Sub-Agent / Helper Agents
================================================================================

STANDARD AGENT FEATURES TEMPLATE (APPLIES TO ALL AGENTS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
For consistency each agent should include an expanded "Features" section derived
from the compact `Configuration` line. Fill these fields per-agent as needed.

Fields:
- Separate Dashboard: (true/false) — dedicated UI for the agent.
- Security Layer: (auth, roles, encryption, SSO, MFA) — access controls and policies.
- Communication Channels:
  - Call: (PBX/IVR settings, call routing, recording)
  - Chat System: (chat channels, livechat integration, web widget)
  - SMS: (provider, number, templates, two-way)
  - Voice & Phone Number: (number(s), TTS voice, IVR scripts)
  - Recording & Script: (recording retention, consent, transcript settings)
  - Location & Country: (allowed regions, timezones, formatting)
- Company Setup: (profile, products, pricing, negotiation rules)
- General Info: (Name, Role, Availability, Personality, Tone, Voice)
- Model & Language: (model name, family, version, primary language, fallbacks)
- Timing & Scheduling:
  - Business Hours: (UTC offsets, holidays)
  - Waiting Duration for Call: (seconds/minutes)
  - Appointment & Scheduling: (calendars, rules, timezone handling)
- Pricing & Negotiation:
  - Pricing Model: (fixed/hourly/usage)
  - Price Limit & Negotiation Rules: (limits, concession rules)
- Integrations: (CRM, ticketing, calendar, telephony, MCP connectors)
- Responsibilities & Routing: (task routing rules, escalation paths)
- Tasks & Work Management:
  - Assigned Tasks: (task list, SLA, dependencies)
  - Remaining Task Completion: (progress metric)
- Behaviour & Limitations: (do/ don't, safe-guards, refusal templates)
- Performance & Insights:
  - Metrics Collected: (latency, accuracy, success-rate)
  - Reporting: (dashboards, scheduled reports)
- Summary & Notes: (freeform summaries, human notes)
- Predictive Layers: (forecasting models, trigger conditions)
- Rules & Regulations: (compliance, legal constraints, regional rules)
- Memory: (short-term/session, long-term, retention policy, purge rules)
- Setup Company (detailed): (profile setup, product & pricing, experience goals, training plan, knowledge base, voice/personality tuning, business hours, additional configs)
- 2-Step Verification: (MFA for critical actions, device check)
- Import & Export Data: (CSV/JSON endpoints, export schedule, data retention)
- Reports: (types, cadence, delivery channels)
- Integrations & MCP: (MCP connectors, API specs, mapping)

Example (expanded entry for an agent):
Configuration: Separate Dashboard | Security Layer | Call | Chat System | Company Setup | ...
Features:
  - Separate Dashboard: true — admin & ops dashboards with role views.
  - Security Layer: SSO via SAML, role-based ACL, data encryption at rest.
  - Call: Twilio integration, IVR menu, call recording retention 90 days.
  - Chat System: Web widget + Slack + Intercom integration.
  - General Info: Name: AI Chief Customer Officer; Role: CX Strategy; Availability: 24/5; Personality: professional, concise.
  - Model & Language: LLM-X v2; Primary: en-US; Fallback: LLM-Y.
  - Pricing: Fixed monthly tier + per-minute call surcharge; Price Limit: $5000; Negotiation: auto-propose up to 10% discount.
  - Memory: session 30 minutes; long-term 365 days; privacy: PII redaction enabled.
  - Integrations & MCP: CRM: Salesforce, Tickets: Zendesk, MCP: connector v1.2

Use this template to expand and document each agent's `Configuration` entries.


